// Result submission / verification / reconciliation (audit gap fix):
// the Examinations Officer's tracking layer over an already-scheduled
// Exam sitting. This model does NOT store a score -- the score of
// record stays on Grade, owned by the Instructor
// (app/api/instructor/portal/grades/route.js) and never written by
// this workflow. Instead it records that this specific Exam's results
// have been collected from the instructor and reconciled against the
// matching Grade bucket for the course+term (targetGradeField reuses
// Grade's own bucket names -- quiz1/quiz2/midterm/final -- so it's
// explicit which bucket this exam's sitting maps to; a course can
// have several MIDTERM-type Exam rows in one term, e.g. a resit, so
// the mapping lives per-Exam rather than assuming one midterm per
// course+term). One row per Exam -- a single verification pass is all
// one sitting needs -- created the first time an Examinations Officer
// opens the reconciliation view for that exam (see
// app/api/examinations/results/route.ts), and updated (never
// duplicated) when they mark it verified/reconciled or add a
// discrepancy note. If a real discrepancy is found, the fix goes
// through the existing, controlled GradeCorrection workflow
// (app/api/records/grade-corrections/route.ts, owned by Academic
// Records/Registrar) -- this table only tracks that the check
// happened, it is never a shortcut to editing Grade itself.
model ExamResultSubmission {
  id              String                   @id @default(cuid())
  examId          String                   @unique
  targetGradeField String
  status          ExamResultStatus         @default(PENDING)
  note            String?                  @db.Text
  verifiedByUserId String?
  verifiedAt      DateTime?
  createdAt       DateTime                 @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime                 @updatedAt

  exam Exam @relation(fields: [examId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@index([status])
}

enum ExamResultStatus {
  PENDING
  SUBMITTED
  VERIFIED
  RECONCILED
}

// Instructor-scheduled virtual class sessions — the real backing store
// for both the Instructor Portal's "Live Classes" tool and the Student
// Portal's "Live Classes" tab, which previously showed unrelated
// hardcoded demo sessions. Scoped to a course exactly like Exam and
// Assignment: any student with an Enrollment in the course sees the
// session, and only an instructor with a matching InstructorCourse
// assignment may create, edit, or cancel it.
